   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] mixture model DIC",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "This is the Stan mailing list.  I&#39;d suggest\r<br>writing to the JAGS list for help with JAGS:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/?source=navbar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/?source%3Dnavbar&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457824355000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33bskwYploHzCda9iJY3M4\">https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/?source=navbar</a>\r<br>\r<br>And maybe reading Aki et al.&#39;s paper on Bayesian alternatives\r<br>to DIC:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.04544\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.04544&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457824355000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23LNkp9Jl0tPpUJfyukPvb\">https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.04544</a>\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>&gt; On Apr 14, 2017, at 5:54 AM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">a.kordba...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; HI EVERYBODY\r<br>&gt; i wrote code model DIC mixture gb2 with 2 component.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; i dont mount DIC. \r<br>&gt; hello \r<br>&gt; my name is alireza kordbagheri of shahid beheshti university tehran.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; i have two question of you:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; can you help me for my question:\r<br>&gt; one question: i read your article tittle:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; i dont know, how draw heatmap ANOVA GAMMA.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; two question:i writing code model with JAGS softwar.\r<br>&gt; i used of function GB2.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I have problem, what DIC estimation?\r<br>&gt; This article is open access at\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ba/1340370933\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ba/1340370933&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457824355000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2x2-meYLyuQSEccpojXnu0\">https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ba/1340370933</a>.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; library(rjags)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; cat(file = &quot;model.txt&quot;,\r<br>&gt; &quot;\r<br>&gt; data {\r<br>&gt;   C &lt;- 100\r<br>&gt;   for (i in 1:N) {\r<br>&gt;     zeros[i] &lt;- 0\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; model {\r<br>&gt;   for (i in 1:N) {\r<br>&gt;     zeros[i] ~ dpois(loglik[i] + C)\r<br>&gt;     loglik[i] &lt;- -log(pi[1] * l1[i] + pi[2] * l2[i])\r<br>&gt;     l1[i] &lt;- abs(a[1]) * pow(y[i], a[1] * p[1] - 1) / (pow(b1[i], a[1] * p[1]) * exp(loggam(p[1]) + loggam(q[1]) - loggam(p[1] + q[1])) * pow(1 + pow(y[i] / b1[i], a[1]), p[1] + q[1]))\r<br>&gt;     l2[i] &lt;- abs(a[2]) * pow(y[i], a[2] * p[2] - 1) / (pow(b2[i], a[2] * p[2]) * exp(loggam(p[2]) + loggam(q[2]) - loggam(p[2] + q[2])) * pow(1 + pow(y[i] / b2[i], a[2]), p[2] + q[2]))\r<br>&gt;     b1[i]&lt;- exp(mu[1] + alpha[1] * f[i] + beta1[1] * col1[i] + beta2[1] * col2[i] + beta3[1] * col3[i] + loggam(p[1]) + loggam(q[1]) - loggam(p[1] + 1 / a[1]) - loggam(q[1] - 1 / a[1]))\r<br>&gt;     b2[i]&lt;- exp(mu[2] + alpha[2] * f[i] + beta1[2] * col1[i] + beta2[2] * col2[i] + beta3[2] * col3[i] + loggam(p[2]) + loggam(q[2]) - loggam(p[2] + 1 / a[2]) - loggam(q[2] - 1 / a[2]))\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt;   pi[1] ~ dunif(0, 1)\r<br>&gt;   pi[2] &lt;- 1 - pi[1]\r<br>&gt;   for(k in 1:2) {\r<br>&gt;     mu[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     alpha[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     beta1[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     beta2[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     beta3[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     a[k] ~ dnorm(0, .01)\r<br>&gt;     p[k] ~ dgamma(.01, .01)I(0, 90)\r<br>&gt;     q[k] ~ dgamma(.01, .001)I(1, 3.5)\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; &quot;)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; data &lt;- matrix(c(\r<br>&gt; 3323,  5, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt; 8332,  8, 0, 1, 1,\r<br>&gt; 9572,  5, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt; 10172, 10, 1, 0, 1,\r<br>&gt; 7631,  2, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt; 3855,  9, 0, 1, 1,\r<br>&gt; 3252,  6, 1, 0, 1,\r<br>&gt; 4433,  8, 0, 1, 1,\r<br>&gt; 2188,  7, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt;   333,  4, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt;   199,  3, 0, 1, 1,\r<br>&gt;   692,  9, 0, 1, 0,\r<br>&gt;   311, 12, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt; 0.01,  5, 1, 0, 1,\r<br>&gt;   405,  6, 0, 1, 0,\r<br>&gt;   293,  6, 0, 1, 0,\r<br>&gt;   76,  7, 1, 0, 1,\r<br>&gt;   14,  9, 1, 0, 0,\r<br>&gt; 3785, 21, 0, 1, 1,\r<br>&gt; 10342, 11, 0, 1, 1), ncol = 5, byrow = TRUE)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; bugs.data &lt;- list(N = nrow(data),\r<br>&gt;                   y = data[, 1],\r<br>&gt;                   f = data[, 2],\r<br>&gt;                   col1 = data[, 3],\r<br>&gt;                   col2 = data[, 4],\r<br>&gt;                   col3 = data[, 5])\r<br>&gt; set.seed(123)\r<br>&gt; inits &lt;- lapply(1:3, function(i) {\r<br>&gt;     list(mu = rnorm(2, 0, 1),\r<br>&gt;         alpha = rnorm(2, 0, 1),\r<br>&gt;         beta1 = rnorm(2, 0, 1),\r<br>&gt;         beta2 = rnorm(2, 0, 1),\r<br>&gt;         beta3 = rnorm(2, 0, 1),\r<br>&gt;         pi = c(runif(1, 0, 1), NA),\r<br>&gt;         a = runif(2, -4, -2),\r<br>&gt;         p = runif(2, 1, 2),\r<br>&gt;         q = runif(2, 1, 2),\r<br>&gt;         .RNG.name = &quot;base::Mersenne-Twister&quot;,\r<br>&gt;         .RNG.seed = i)\r<br>&gt;     })\r<br>&gt; pars &lt;- c(&quot;mu&quot;, &quot;alpha&quot;, &quot;beta1&quot;, &quot;beta2&quot;, &quot;beta3&quot;, &quot;pi&quot;,\r<br>&gt;           &quot;a&quot;, &quot;p&quot;, &quot;q&quot;)\r<br>&gt; model &lt;- jags.model(&quot;model.txt&quot;,\r<br>&gt;                     data = bugs.data,\r<br>&gt;                     inits = inits,\r<br>&gt;                     n.chains = 3,\r<br>&gt;                     n.adapt = 1000)\r<br>&gt; update(model, 3000)\r<br>&gt; samp &lt;- coda.samples(model,\r<br>&gt;                     variable.names = pars,\r<br>&gt;                     n.iter = 4000, thin = 4)\r<br>&gt; gelman.diag(samp, multivariate = FALSE)\r<br>&gt; traceplot(samp[, 15]) # pi[1]\r<br>&gt; traceplot(samp[, 16]) # pi[2]\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; can you help me.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Regards,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
